x86_64-linux  a closure type as a template argument: clang numbers the closures of main by its own count ($_0 where cxx1 writes $_2 on Itanium) and spells them <lambda_N> on the Microsoft ABI, where cxx1 writes $_N - the closure naming lambda.nonames records, not this case's subject; what the case is about, classes over a closure type made from the read, is checked by run.sh and -check=templates.
